<SCENARIO VER="105">
{CREATECG "プレート" "グラフィック\システム\立木三日プレート.gal" "NORMAL" "#1" "180" "380" "600" "1" "100" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{MESON "500"}
<TXSPN>Oh? Erina Goto is the culprit, you say.<PG>
The latter half followed the incident from Erina Goto's viewpoint, but there was a scene where part of her viewpoint was missing entirely, was there not.<PG>
Yes, from when Haruka Niimura killed herself until waking up in the hospital.<PG>
It would be good if we knew what happened during that time, but conveniently, it is <STYLE ID="1" RUBY="・・">only</STYLE> that part she does not remember. This, too, is a strange matter.<PG>
At the end she seems to have hit upon the truth, but perhaps she realized that she herself had been involved in the incident by some means.<PG>
The Erina Goto culprit theory, I like it.<PG>
{}
<EVENT VALUE="MESEND">
